# Automation — non-negotiable

You must run chores yourself. **Never tell the user to run lint/build/sync unless `verify` is blocked by environment limits.**

## Before marking ANY task complete

```sh
npm run verify
```

If it fails: fix the failure, re-run until green. Include synced agent files in the same change set.

## After route or script changes

`npm run verify` runs `sync:agent --check`. If it fails, run `npm run sync:agent` and commit:

- `llms.txt`
- `AGENTS.md` (scripts table)
- `docs/generated/manifest.json`

## Do not skip

- ESLint (`lint` inside verify)
- Production build (`build` inside verify)
- Agent manifest sync check
- Updating agent docs when architecture/commands change

## Perf work

Run `npm run verify:ci` or rely on CI perf job; cite `perf-reports/latest.json` metrics.

## Commits

Only commit when the user asks. When committing, hooks run automatically — ensure `verify` passed first so pre-push does not fail.

See [docs/AUTOMATION.md](docs/AUTOMATION.md).
